  "description": {
    "ja": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 日本語版「ヒメモダマ」",
      "source_url": "https://ja.wikipedia.org/wiki/%E3%83%92%E3%83%A1%E3%83%A2%E3%83%80%E3%83%9E",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 110950393,
      "text": "ヒメモダマ はマメ科モダマ属のつる性常緑樹。別名：コウシュンモダマ、方言名：ウジルカンダ、スバガーニー。環境省及び沖縄県カテゴリー 準絶滅危惧種（NT）。学名はE. koshunensisとされることもある。同属のモダマ と混同されることがあるが、別種である。"
    },
    "en": {
      "source": "Wikipedia 英語版「Entada phaseoloides」",
      "source_url": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Entada_phaseoloides",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "license_url": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/",
      "retrieved": "2026-10-09",
      "revision": 1367360346,
      "text": "Entada phaseoloides, commonly known in English as the matchbox bean or St. Thomas' bean, is a large twining vine or liana in the pea and bean family Fabaceae, native to a broad area of Asia-Pacific, from China to northern Australia and the southwestern Pacific."
    }
